# Behaviour fixture for GithubExporterPartialData (homelab#1405) — validates that the alert
# correctly fires when partial-data errors occur AND the PR series is absent, and stays silent
# when either condition does not hold.
#
# Fix round 2 findings (arbitration 2026-09-05T11:09:30Z):
#   1. `by (job)` was dropping the `class` label → changed to `by (job, class)` so the label
#      survives to the annotation
#   2. The right-hand side `(count by (job) (github_pull_request_open) == 0 or absent(…))` never
#      matched — `count` over an absent series returns empty vector (never 0), and `absent()` has
#      no labels to match against `job`. Fixed to `and on() absent(github_pull_request_open)`.
#   3. The expression is now testable: alert fires when counter increments AND PR family is absent,
#      stays silent when either condition does not hold.
#
#   devbox run -- promtool test rules argocd/resources/github-exporter/partial-data.promtool-test
#
# Named .promtool-test, not .yaml: manifest-lint kubeconforms every *.yaml under argocd/resources.
#
groups:
  - name: github-partial-data
    rules:
      - alert: GithubExporterPartialData
        expr: (max by (job, class) (increase(github_exporter_graphql_partial_total[15m])) > 0) and on() absent(github_pull_request_open)
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "github-exporter: GraphQL partial data — PR series missing"
          description: "GraphQL walk returned partial data (class: {{ $labels.class }}) in the last 15m and the entire `github_pull_request_*` series family is absent from Prometheus. The review edge, codeowner-park watcher and behind-dispatcher are dark (FU-108 class — the read succeeds with nothing in it). Check: the `class` label says which path to follow — `resource-limit` → the walk's nested `first:` fan-out against GitHub's query-cost ceiling, see github-exporter.py; `not-accessible` → the exporter PAT's repo access (scripts/github-exporter-pat-bootstrap.sh, docs/github-setup.md §Tokens); `other` → the pod log's field errors. githubstatus.com rules out a GitHub-side outage. The */15 reflex + coordinate CronWorkflow backstops own re-reviews and CI-reds meanwhile."
